One could also consider changes to the scoring system.

As a YANI, what if only the first N monsters killed are worth
full score? (Or, all monsters killed until turn T).  After that,
you receive some fraction or dwindling return. This would amount
to an ascension speed bonus, and some extinctionist games might
end up with a lower score than a straight ascension.

So score would reflect the toughness of the monsters you are
facing up until a certain point where you're probably just
goofing off and not really in any danger. If you want to mix
in conducts, perhaps (for example) when you break wishless
T or N decreases by some number. Breaking a conduct means
you're expected to ascend even sooner). Personally however
I think that conducts should not be reflected in scoring at
all.

If you wanted to clamp down entirely on repeated kills of
unique monsters you could also do that by rewarding full
points only the first time. This might be too restrictive
though.

